.TH IGADIT-TOOLKIT 8 "2026" "Group 5" "iGADit Administration"
.SH NAME
igadit-toolkit \- administration and operational toolkit for the iGADit GAD document management system
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sudo ./igadit-install.sh
[\-\-help] [SOURCE_PATH]
.br
.B sudo ./igadit-backup.sh
[\-\-help] [DESTINATION_DIR]
.br
.B sudo ./igadit-restore.sh
[\-\-help] [BACKUP_PATH]
.br
.B sudo ./igadit-log-summary.sh
[\-\-help] [OUTPUT_DIR]
.br
.B sudo ./igadit-health-report.sh
[\-\-help]
.br
.B sudo ./igadit-disk-alert.sh
[\-\-help] [THRESHOLD_PERCENT]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The iGADit toolkit comprises six production-grade Bash administration scripts
tailored for the iGADit Document Tracking and Routing System at the Bicol
University Gender and Development (GAD) Office.
The suite automates server provisioning, backup verification, point-in-time
disaster recovery, system and application log aggregation, multi-subsystem
health checks, and proactive storage threshold alerting.
All operational credentials and environment parameters are loaded from an
access-restricted configuration file (/etc/igadit/igadit.conf) governed by
strict file permission masks (0600).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B igadit-install.sh [\-\-help] [SOURCE_PATH]
Deploys the Apache2 web server, PHP 8.2 runtime modules, and MySQL database
platform on a clean Ubuntu Server 24.04 LTS host. Deploys the application
repository, builds the virtual host, generates database schemas, executes
Laravel database migrations, and enforces least-privilege permission masks
across application storage and cache paths.
.TP
.B igadit-backup.sh [\-\-help] [DESTINATION_DIR]
Generates a timestamped backup containing a consistent MySQL database dump
produced via mysqldump, archived alongside the Laravel storage/ tree and environment
configuration file into a unified compressed archive. Verifies archive integrity
and contents using tar inspection routines before reporting success.
.TP
.B igadit-restore.sh [\-\-help] [BACKUP_PATH]
Performs point-in-time disaster recovery by recreating the MySQL schema from an
exported dump, unpacking verified filesystem storage trees, comparing restored
files against the archive via tar -d, normalizing web daemon ownership to www-data,
verifying that restored database table counts match the backup dump, and validating
availability via HTTP status checks within a 10-minute SLA window.
.TP
.B igadit-log-summary.sh [\-\-help] [OUTPUT_DIR]
Parses Apache HTTP access and error logs alongside Laravel storage logs.
Compiles request totals, HTTP client/server error counts, top accessed
URI endpoints, top requesting remote hosts, and recent application exceptions
into a dated report file.
.TP
.B igadit-health-report.sh [\-\-help]
Conducts comprehensive diagnostic assessments across Apache2 and MySQL systemd
service units, disk partition capacity via df, memory allocation via free,
CPU load averages, and HTTP service availability.
.TP
.B igadit-disk-alert.sh [\-\-help] [THRESHOLD_PERCENT]
Evaluates storage partition utilization against a warning threshold (default 80%).
Emits prominent visual terminal warnings, appends timestamps to the system alert log,
lists the top storage-consuming application directories and files, and exits
with status 3 if any threshold is violated.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Deploy platform and application on a fresh host:
.B sudo ./igadit-install.sh
.TP
Create a verified database and filesystem backup:
.B sudo ./igadit-backup.sh
.TP
Perform interactive system disaster recovery:
.B sudo ./igadit-restore.sh
.TP
Generate an administrative log analysis report:
.B sudo ./igadit-log-summary.sh /var/log/reports
.TP
Execute a full server operational health audit:
.B sudo ./igadit-health-report.sh
.TP
Monitor partition capacity with a custom 85% threshold:
.B sudo ./igadit-disk-alert.sh 85
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/igadit/igadit.conf
Global operational configuration file containing database credentials,
paths, and threshold limits. Owned by root:root with mode 0600.
.TP
.I /var/www/html/igadit/
Root application directory for the deployed Laravel codebase.
.TP
.I /var/www/html/igadit/storage/
Application document storage and log path. Owned by www-data:www-data.
.TP
.I /var/backups/igadit/
Default archive repository containing timestamped database and file snapshots.
.TP
.I /var/log/apache2/
Apache HTTP server access and error logs.
.TP
.I /var/www/html/igadit/storage/logs/laravel.log
Application diagnostic and exception error log.
.TP
.I /var/log/igadit-disk-alert.log
Append-only log recording threshold alert events.
.TP
.I /var/log/igadit-reports/
Default output repository for log summary reports.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success. Operation completed without errors.
.TP
.B 1
Privilege check failed (root privileges required).
.TP
.B 2
Configuration file (/etc/igadit/igadit.conf) not found.
.TP
.B 3
Execution failure, resource warning, or threshold exceeded.
.TP
.B 4
Invalid command-line argument or user cancellation.
.TP
.B 5
Restoration or database operational failure.
